## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.ts** (`applyReportDiscountsService`): This function COMPUTES the discount amount that ends up in dispatch.report.price.discount — the exact field that is wrong/missing for return trips. It matches discounts to dispatches by comparing dispatch lineItem.id to the order lineItem.id stored in the discount. For return trip tickets, the Mozio dispatch line items have IDs generated via getDispatchLineItemKey (a composite key) that do NOT match the original BigCommerce order line item IDs, so the filter finds zero matching discounts and the promo amount is never applied to the return dispatch.
  - **Minimal fix:** The filter on line 21-23 compares Mozio dispatch lineItem.id (a composite key from getDispatchLineItemKey) against discount.lineItemId (the original BigCommerce order line item ID). For return trips these never match, so discountsForDispatch is empty and the discount is skipped. The fix: change the matching to use the order line item ID that is carried on the dispatch line item (e.g. lineItem.orderLineItemId or equivalent field), or pre-build a lookup map from dispatch line item key → order line item ID using the same getDispatchLineItemKey function that mapOrderDispatchesToMozioDispatches uses, so the comparison becomes order-line-item-ID to order-line-item-ID. If the dispatch line item carries the original order line item ID as a separate field, compare against that field instead of lineItem.id.


